command:
& 'C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe' issue reopen 654 --repo organicoverlords/regression-research; $body=@'
Reopened: direct user32 visibility proof showed the first fix was incomplete. A manual `pythonw.exe timeline_materializer.py refresh --quiet` run attributed child processes by parent PID and observed 8 direct `git.exe` children with `IsWindowVisible=True`; `gh.exe` children were hidden. `CREATE_NO_WINDOW` alone is therefore insufficient for Git for Windows on this path. Continuing the same acceptance identity with an explicit Windows hidden `STARTUPINFO`/`SW_HIDE` launch policy and a regression test that proves the startup flags, then re-running direct visibility proof before re-enabling the task.
'@; $file=Join-Path $env:TEMP ('issue654-reopen-'+[guid]::NewGuid().ToString('N')+'.md'); Set-Content $file $body -Encoding utf8; try { & 'C:\Program Files\GitHub CLI\gh.exe' issue comment 654 --repo organicoverlords/regression-research --body-file $file } finally { Remove-Item $file -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue }
